#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059797 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059596 :question/id #uuid "822f40ce-c449-5193-9585-8fea63d0db67" :question/math-academy-id "e-5167" :question/problem "Nine years ago, an organization had $4\\,350$ members. Today it has $7\\,210$ members. What was its continuously compounded rate of growth during this nine-year period? Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." :question/worked-solution "The continuously compounded growth equation is\n\n$$\nP = P_0e^{rt}\n$$\n\nWe have an initial amount of $P_0=4\\,350$, a final amount of $P=7\\,210$, and a time duration of $t=9$ years. Substituting these values into the formula and solving for $r$, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{array}{rl}\\displaystyle P & \\displaystyle  = {P}_{0} {e}^{r t} \\\\ \\displaystyle 7 \\hspace{0.167em} 210 & \\displaystyle  = ( 4 \\hspace{0.167em} 350 ) {e}^{r ( 9 )} \\\\ \\displaystyle {e}^{9 r} & \\displaystyle  = {\\displaystyle \\frac{7 \\hspace{0.167em} 210}{4 \\hspace{0.167em} 350}} \\\\ \\displaystyle {e}^{9 r} & \\displaystyle  = 1.657 \\hspace{0.167em} 47. . . \\\\ \\displaystyle \\ln   ( {e}^{9 r} ) & \\displaystyle  = \\ln   ( 1.657 \\hspace{0.167em} 47. . . ) \\\\ \\displaystyle 9 r & \\displaystyle  = 0.505 \\hspace{0.167em} 29. . . \\\\ \\displaystyle r & \\displaystyle  = 0.056 \\hspace{0.167em} 14. . . \\approx  5.6 \\mathrm{\\% } .\\end{array}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, continuously compounded rate of growth is $5.6\\%$."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c0a7b30-b6b4-584e-9816-506f8ec00813" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050649 :topic/encompasses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429668 :encompassing/rationale "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 1 eligible passed source activities = 1.000000; nearest selected fraction = 1. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1 (1/1). Selection: most observations, then lower