:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$24$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056697} {:answer/id #uuid "e754e946-5a50-5695-8fd9-d0255075e26b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$9$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056698} {:answer/id #uuid "f6ae3e91-7a63-5c55-9b7b-46b048910899" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$17$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056699}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e15eba41-5d19-5f72-9e11-b8af0663fb46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$24$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056697} :answer-field/id #uuid "2696e4f7-9b9d-5587-962c-5a7464928448" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056694}] :question/id #uuid "6b547ba8-6bef-5f97-b295-98d6170d064b" :question/math-academy-id "q-1434" :question/problem "There are currently $102$ koalas living in a secluded forest, but their population is decreasing at a continuously compounded rate of $9.5 \\mathrm{\\% }$ per year. How many years must pass for there to be only $10$ koalas left in that forest? Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The continuously compounded growth equation is $P=P_0e^{rt}$. Here $P_0=102$, $P=10$, and $r=-0.095$ per year. Solve for $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n10 &= 102e^{-0.095t} \\\\\ne^{-0.095t} &= \\frac{10}{102} \\\\\n-0.095t &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{10}{102}\\right) \\\\\nt &= \\frac{\\ln(10/102)}{-0.095} \\\\\n&\\approx 24.4462.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest integer gives $24$ years."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060057 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88f2af79-a331-5ae8-90bc-d53f50e99972" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$31 \\mathrm{\\% }$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056701} {:answer/id #uuid "9482c2bf-1cbb-559a-81b2-9a8ad1367a8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$21 \\mathrm{\\% }$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056702} {:answer/id #uuid "d4a0610f-c16c-56b5-9218-a2bd11d277fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$42 \\mathrm{\\% }$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056703} {:answer/id #uuid "1c444bc1-f2e7-5996-a836-c9dcd838cfd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$34 \\mathrm{\\% }$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056704} {:answer/id #uuid "644cd3ca-56c7-5044-9fdf-4a07582bf186" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$26 \\mathrm{\\% }$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056705}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88f2af79-a331-5ae8-90bc-d53f50e99972" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$31 \\mathrm{\\% }$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056701} :answer-field/id #uuid "2eeed5ec-b57f-5841-9c2b-8acd8925f55c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056700}] :question/id #uuid "f32196ff-a1c3-58c8-8249-0c13bdced6e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-1435" :question/problem "In a biology class, the teacher began the experiment with $10$ bacteria in a petri dish. After $14$ minutes, the number of bacteria increased to $781$. What was the continuously compounded growth rate of the bacteria? Round your answer to the nearest percent.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The continuously compounded growth equation is $P=P_0e^{rt}$. Here $P_0=10$, $P=781$, and $t=14$ minutes. Solve for $r$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n781 &= 10e^{14r} \\\\\ne^{14r} &= \\frac{781}{10} \\\\\n14r &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{781}{10}\\right) \\\\\nr &= \\frac{\\ln(781/10)}{14} \\\\\n&\\approx 0.311285.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe percentage rate is approximately $31.1285\\%$ per minute. Rounding to the nearest percent gives $31\\%$ per minute."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676439 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09641951-6f9f-560e-90d6-a38906dbfbcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$59\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676427} {:answer/id #uuid "0fdabe40-9d46-5fcb-a4e1-e747db4a20f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$63\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676429} {:answer/id #uuid "1ac7ed7d-f216-5202-a671-de9804a5bf3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$66\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676430} {:answer/id #uuid "b927e458-2bce-52df-98cc-ba16ce53c7d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$73\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676452} {:answer/id #uuid "dc286a52-d8df-5097-837a-4fe2ba2b4384" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$76\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676458}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09641951-6f9f-560e-90d6-a38906dbfbcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$59\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676427} :answer-field/id #uuid "51528e61-5192-5672-a989-0d2e5e3adf70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676436}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "663ef7a5-cfb7-5c1b-8989-14764743962d" :question/problem "In a biology class, the teacher began the experiment with $14$ bacteria in a petri dish. After $6$ minutes, the number of bacteria increased to $471$. What was the continuously compounded growth rate of the bacteria? Round your answer to the nearest percent.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "The initial population is $P_0=14$, the final population is $P=471$, and the elapsed time is $t=6$ minutes. The decimal rate $r$ is per minute.\n\nUse the continuously compounded growth equation, isolate the exponential, take natural logarithms, and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= P_0e^{rt} \\\\\n471 &= 14e^{6r} \\\\\ne^{6r} &= \\frac{471}{14} \\\\\n\\ln\\left(e^{6r}\\right) &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{471}{14}\\right) \\\\\n6r &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{471}{14}\\right) \\\\\nr &= \\frac{\\ln\\left(\\frac{471}{14}\\right)}{6} \\\\\nr &\\approx 0.5859668 \\\\\n100r &\\approx 58.59668\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConverting the decimal rate to a percentage and rounding to the nearest percent gives approximately $59\\%$ per minute."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676440 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0df2a44c-a3c5-57ae-9fab-bef5ffaedbc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$66$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676428} {:answer/id #uuid "27d5d874-cb66-5118-950c-7de55172b579" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$51$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676431} {:answer/id #uuid "2d19eecb-2fd3-580f-94d0-a18642e0e65d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$63$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676433} {:answer/id #uuid "a1c0bd23-0a64-5a3d-a456-e571389085d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$60$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676449} {:answer/id #uuid "c7f5981a-88b4-5a77-999d-8d8e0117bb73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$59$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676454}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d19eecb-2fd3-580f-94d0-a18642e0e65d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$63$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676433} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c7d1826-33db-5f83-96f3-289163044da2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676446}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6d7e06f3-f89c-5ef4-9cfc-ef54a65f8fdc" :question/problem "There are currently $592$ koalas living in a secluded forest, but their population is decreasing at a continuously compounded rate of $4.3\\%$ per year. How many years must pass for there to be only $40$ koalas left in that forest? Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "The initial population is $P_0=592$ and the final population is $P=40$. A decrease of $4.3\\%$ per year means $r=-0.043$, with $t$ in years.\n\nUse the continuously compounded growth equation, isolate the exponential, take natural logarithms, and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= P_0e^{rt} \\\\\n40 &= 592e^{-0.043t} \\\\\ne^{-0.043t} &= \\frac{40}{592} \\\\\n\\ln\\left(e^{-0.043t}\\right) &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{40}{592}\\right) \\\\\n-0.043t &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{40}{592}\\right) \\\\\nt &= \\frac{\\ln\\left(\\frac{40}{592}\\right)}{-0.043} \\\\\nt &\\approx 62.66575 \\\\\nt &\\approx 63\\text{ years}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the time is approximately $63$ years."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676442 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ac01d59-0302-592a-af99-14e05a3d3adf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$81$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676432} {:answer/id #uuid "43132a69-ebf9-5aec-b2d0-49976b90d326" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$72$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676435} {:answer/id #uuid "5cc9fdbb-f192-5a52-b0b5-145a3df2f526" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$73$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676438} {:answer/id #uuid "c91e1e7b-8997-5084-a5a2-eff7314ad5d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$74$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676456} {:answer/id #uuid "daa70773-bb0e-50fd-8323-de9534310480" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$82$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676457}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "daa70773-bb0e-50fd-8323-de9534310480" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$82$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676457} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8913028-e23f-5e22-ba47-e411ba1a3285" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676455}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "85630d86-d703-5b7d-8f7c-82164c47f0af" :question/problem "There are currently $340$ koalas living in a secluded forest, but their population is decreasing at a continuously compounded rate of $2.6\\%$ per year. How many years must pass for there to be only $40$ koalas left in that forest? Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "The initial population is $P_0=340$ and the final population is $P=40$. A decrease of $2.6\\%$ per year means $r=-0.026$, with $t$ in years.\n\nUse the continuously compounded growth equation, isolate the exponential, take natural logarithms, and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= P_0e^{rt} \\\\\n40 &= 340e^{-0.026t} \\\\\ne^{-0.026t} &= \\frac{40}{340} \\\\\n\\ln\\left(e^{-0.026t}\\right) &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{40}{340}\\right) \\\\\n-0.026t &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{40}{340}\\right) \\\\\nt &= \\frac{\\ln\\left(\\frac{40}{340}\\right)}{-0.026} \\\\\nt &\\approx 82.31024 \\\\\nt &\\approx 82\\text{ years}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the time is approximately $82$ years."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676450 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e930e26-1a78-59cd-adb9-c50da6422bbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$24\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676434} {:answer/id #uuid "85638b41-2bdc-5b75-8215-f41f77d23ba8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$15\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676443} {:answer/id #uuid "8c210b49-6903-59fa-9108-4d09e26a3aeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$22\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676444} {:answer/id #uuid "9f26c109-d3b7-59c5-bdb4-37f5547e2fd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$21\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676447} {:answer/id #uuid "9f8da3f1-a40f-5b6b-932d-c550d0d0f90f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$17\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f26c109-d3b7-59c5-bdb4-37f5547e2fd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$21\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676447} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba2b0173-6de4-533c-a827-1926029684cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676453}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ac53e8b2-646f-5fdc-bc8b-13c00bef0b23" :question/problem "In a biology class, the teacher began the experiment with $26$ bacteria in a petri dish. After $16$ minutes, the number of bacteria increased to $788$. What was the continuously compounded growth rate of the bacteria? Round your answer to the nearest percent.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "The initial population is $P_0=26$, the final population is $P=788$, and the elapsed time is $t=16$ minutes. The decimal rate $r$ is per minute.\n\nUse the continuously compounded growth equation, isolate the exponential, take natural logarithms, and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= P_0e^{rt} \\\\\n788 &= 26e^{16r} \\\\\ne^{16r} &= \\frac{788}{26} \\\\\n\\ln\\left(e^{16r}\\right) &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{788}{26}\\right) \\\\\n16r &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{788}{26}\\right) \\\\\nr &= \\frac{\\ln\\left(\\frac{788}{26}\\right)}{16} \\\\\nr &\\approx 0.2132126 \\\\\n100r &\\approx 21.32126\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConverting the decimal rate to a percentage and rounding to the nearest percent gives approximately $21\\%$ per minute."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676460 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "560ce953-716c-572b-8b78-160be89e305f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$36\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676437} {:answer/id #uuid "747319cc-5363-51bc-a1ed-edb5bc3e4f3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$13\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676441} {:answer/id #uuid "936a07dd-1862-55d6-b676-7aa50a4d926a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$28\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676445} {:answer/id #uuid "b71ab703-9cdb-56f6-be65-a14b0576a3f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$11\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676451} {:answer/id #uuid "e0dd8a70-7452-54d2-9516-d421e5747dd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$21\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "560ce953-716c-572b-8b78-160be89e305f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$36\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676437} :answer-field/id #uuid "06a322ec-f56d-5b73-bc52-de3a78adca05" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676426}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f65cff61-9251-5afe-a2f7-67b2d162f9e7" :question/problem "In a biology class, the teacher began the experiment with $26$ bacteria in a petri dish. After $8$ minutes, the number of bacteria increased to $470$. What was the continuously compounded growth rate of the bacteria? Round your answer to the nearest percent.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "The initial population is $P_0=26$, the final population is $P=470$, and the elapsed time is $t=8$ minutes. The decimal rate $r$ is per minute.\n\nUse the continuously compounded growth equation, isolate the exponential, take natural logarithms, and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= P_0e^{rt} \\\\\n470 &= 26e^{8r} \\\\\ne^{8r} &= \\frac{470}{26} \\\\\n\\ln\\left(e^{8r}\\right) &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{470}{26}\\right) \\\\\n8r &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{470}{26}\\right) \\\\\nr &= \\frac{\\ln\\left(\\frac{470}{26}\\right)}{8} \\\\\nr &\\approx 0.3618295 \\\\\n100r &\\approx 36.18295\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConverting the decimal rate to a percentage and rounding to the nearest percent gives approximately $36\\%$ per minute."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718601 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2504313d-b288-5df3-8cdc-0fd8dfc044e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$67\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718592} {:answer/id #uuid "3a084adf-b930-5b02-b48d-c8a7cfce2cd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$77\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718594} {:answer/id #uuid "573ca87e-b81a-5c0e-b878-5f5403e71553" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$74\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718598} {:answer/id #uuid "7b4017a4-42e9-5326-a589-4eec872a59aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$83\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718606} {:answer/id #uuid "eaf162e4-3acf-5b86-93bc-5b7a27c58e2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$71\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a084adf-b930-5b02-b48d-c8a7cfce2cd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$77\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718594} :answer-field/id #uuid "5886e3c9-2962-546e-b42b-4cd2bbbe535d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718599}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6282714f-86f7-539d-8dcf-29f522eab8ab" :question/problem "In a biology class, the teacher began the experiment with $14$ bacteria in a petri dish. After $5$ minutes, the number of bacteria increased to $658$. What was the continuously compounded growth rate of the bacteria? Round your answer to the nearest percent.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The initial population is $P_0=14$, the final population is $P=658$, and the elapsed time is $t=5$ minutes. The decimal rate $r$ is per minute.\n\nUse the continuously compounded growth equation, isolate the exponential, take natural logarithms, and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= P_0e^{rt} \\\\\n658 &= 14e^{5r} \\\\\ne^{5r} &= \\frac{658}{14} \\\\\n\\ln\\left(e^{5r}\\right) &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{658}{14}\\right) \\\\\n5r &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{658}{14}\\right) \\\\\nr &= \\frac{\\ln\\left(\\frac{658}{14}\\right)}{5} \\\\\nr &\\approx 0.7700295 \\\\\n100r &\\approx 77.00295\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConverting the decimal rate to a percentage and rounding to the nearest percent gives approximately $77\\%$ per minute."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718605 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0822be71-2c04-5d27-b42f-62e8fe74b25e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$22\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718589} {:answer/id #uuid "170d0680-a11f-55df-b42b-ffc13dd8fdcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$33\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718590} {:answer/id #uuid "60a3693b-c84e-5489-821d-08e118be639f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$30\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718600} {:answer/id #uuid "9718cd12-6a3a-59f8-9358-ca178c4f0045" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$19\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718610} {:answer/id #uuid "99891059-8278-5f3d-bad3-bf3531b618f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$14\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99891059-8278-5f3d-bad3-bf3531b618f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$14\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718611} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6e01186-83ec-5681-9bc8-c56b5eedba65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718614}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7ad32226-32ee-52d3-ad07-c7cf248ffbb3" :question/problem "In a biology class, the teacher began the experiment with $25$ bacteria in a petri dish. After $14$ minutes, the number of bacteria increased to $184$. What was the continuously compounded growth rate of the bacteria? Round your answer to the nearest percent.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The initial population is $P_0=25$, the final population is $P=184$, and the elapsed time is $t=14$ minutes. The decimal rate $r$ is per minute.\n\nUse the continuously compounded growth equation, isolate the exponential, take natural logarithms, and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= P_0e^{rt} \\\\\n184 &= 25e^{14r} \\\\\ne^{14r} &= \\frac{184}{25} \\\\\n\\ln\\left(e^{14r}\\right) &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{184}{25}\\right) \\\\\n14r &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{184}{25}\\right) \\\\\nr &= \\frac{\\ln\\left(\\frac{184}{25}\\right)}{14} \\\\\nr &\\approx 0.1425757 \\\\\n100r &\\approx 14.25757\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConverting the decimal rate to a percentage and rounding to the nearest percent gives approximately $14\\%$ per minute."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718608 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d6b8174-642d-58e0-ae3d-4406879ea648" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$114$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718597} {:answer/id #uuid "a666c559-f529-56ad-9486-a2b1e8b2db68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$108$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718612} {:answer/id #uuid "ebb1a0bf-293e-56a7-a6cb-2bd758c22d7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$110$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718618} {:answer/id #uuid "ee77ff5d-d3ef-5a08-a02e-371a3435c0e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$112$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718619} {:answer/id #uuid "ef913d26-3ead-5e56-a257-bb5a581f5780" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$116$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718620}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ebb1a0bf-293e-56a7-a6cb-2bd758c22d7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$110$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718618} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb70bd51-1fd8-57f8-b3ab-44c130aa64bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718622}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "88863802-911c-559b-a7a4-c6fd80ee55d9" :question/problem "There are currently $498$ koalas living in a secluded forest, but their population is decreasing at a continuously compounded rate of $3.4\\%$ per year. How many years must pass for there to be only $12$ koalas left in that forest? Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The initial population is $P_0=498$ and the final population is $P=12$. A decrease of $3.4\\%$ per year means $r=-0.034$, with $t$ in years.\n\nUse the continuously compounded growth equation, isolate the exponential, take natural logarithms, and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= P_0e^{rt} \\\\\n12 &= 498e^{-0.034t} \\\\\ne^{-0.034t} &= \\frac{12}{498} \\\\\n\\ln\\left(e^{-0.034t}\\right) &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{12}{498}\\right) \\\\\n-0.034t &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{12}{498}\\right) \\\\\nt &= \\frac{\\ln\\left(\\frac{12}{498}\\right)}{-0.034} \\\\\nt &\\approx 109.57922 \\\\\nt &\\approx 110\\text{ years}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the time is approximately $110$ years."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718616 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d67cb49-009a-566e-9248-70e5577b3dac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$126$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718591} {:answer/id #uuid "32453c9e-4936-5721-9cd7-caa1a1bfe345" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$109$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718593} {:answer/id #uuid "71424a84-6149-5baa-b6ce-545fbc2c40e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$120$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718603} {:answer/id #uuid "752c4308-5934-5c79-a462-64f87f1e0ef9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$116$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718604} {:answer/id #uuid "fdd7f327-f838-5246-9d0d-249524b64271" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$130$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32453c9e-4936-5721-9cd7-caa1a1bfe345" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$109$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718593} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9206112-579e-5e6a-9e48-dcd910b9c49e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718613}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dd13a5ec-3f35-5991-8ad7-2b401a1a0073" :question/problem "There are currently $543$ koalas living in a secluded forest, but their population is decreasing at a continuously compounded rate of $2.9\\%$ per year. How many years must pass for there to be only $23$ koalas left in that forest? Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The initial population is $P_0=543$ and the final population is $P=23$. A decrease of $2.9\\%$ per year means $r=-0.029$, with $t$ in years.\n\nUse the continuously compounded growth equation, isolate the exponential, take natural logarithms, and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= P_0e^{rt} \\\\\n23 &= 543e^{-0.029t} \\\\\ne^{-0.029t} &= \\frac{23}{543} \\\\\n\\ln\\left(e^{-0.029t}\\right) &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{23}{543}\\right) \\\\\n-0.029t &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{23}{543}\\right) \\\\\nt &= \\frac{\\ln\\left(\\frac{23}{543}\\right)}{-0.029} \\\\\nt &\\approx 109.02121 \\\\\nt &\\approx 109\\text{ years}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the time is approximately $109$ years."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718621 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40e81a47-41a8-5efe-b8ba-544e5d50b471" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$57\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718595} {:answer/id #uuid "430db582-af40-570b-a5c3-4ef1c2f0d034" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$64\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718596} {:answer/id #uuid "70786690-4a26-54db-9ea8-72c5999e4729" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$67\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718602} {:answer/id #uuid "7d3a3d21-e3e1-5503-8ce4-d06000037f07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$61\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718607} {:answer/id #uuid "c3fc5218-26f5-564f-b70c-a8e66705d04a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$54\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718615}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d3a3d21-e3e1-5503-8ce4-d06000037f07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$61\\%$ per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718607} :answer-field/id #uuid "890957f7-308f-5ec1-b8ff-30e14a3050ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718609}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f6ec8216-66e5-56d8-884e-056c853ffa5a" :question/problem "In a biology class, the teacher began the experiment with $34$ bacteria in a petri dish. After $7$ minutes, the number of bacteria increased to $2372$. What was the continuously compounded growth rate of the bacteria? Round your answer to the nearest percent.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The initial population is $P_0=34$, the final population is $P=2372$, and the elapsed time is $t=7$ minutes. The decimal rate $r$ is per minute.\n\nUse the continuously compounded growth equation, isolate the exponential, take natural logarithms, and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= P_0e^{rt} \\\\\n2372 &= 34e^{7r} \\\\\ne^{7r} &= \\frac{2372}{34} \\\\\n\\ln\\left(e^{7r}\\right) &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{2372}{34}\\right) \\\\\n7r &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{2372}{34}\\right) \\\\\nr &= \\frac{\\ln\\left(\\frac{2372}{34}\\right)}{7} \\\\\nr &\\approx 0.6064469 \\\\\n100r &\\approx 60.64469\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConverting the decimal rate to a percentage and rounding to the nearest percent gives approximately $61\\%$ per minute."}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Rate or Time Duration"}]}
